# {{ mod_name }}

A compact Galaxy on Fire 2 PC campaign mission starter by {{ author_name }}.

The generated layout deliberately keeps mutable mission state in `state.lua`;
ModAPI adds this directory to Lua's module search path before executing
`init.lua`, so `require("state")` resolves beside the entry point.

Generate into `{{ mod_id | snake_case }}` and copy the folder to the game's
`mods` directory. Review the example system coordinates, linked system ID,
textures, mission gate, dialogue portraits, and reward before shipping a mod.
Created systems, stations, and missions are registered during `EarlyInit`,
matching the API's lifecycle restrictions.

Open the generated folder in Visual Studio Code and install its recommended
Lua extension for ModAPI globals, dialogue and mission table types, signatures,
and hover documentation. See `MODAPI-DEVELOPMENT.md`.

The generated source is GPL-3.0-only and detached from Klonker after
generation.
